Professional Summary
Safe antibiotic practice can be summarized as: diagnose carefully → confirm that an antibiotic is needed → choose the most appropriate agent → prescribe the correct dose, route and duration → check patient-specific factors and interactions → dispense a quality product within expiry and proper storage → counsel clearly → review response → narrow, stop or modify treatment when evidence supports it.
Antibiotics are valuable medicines. Their effectiveness for future patients depends on using them responsibly today.
 
